": {"audiosrc": "engenn5le09ob06re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn5le09ob06re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "", "image": "engenn5le09ob06re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class =\"strong\">Marco</span>: There's only ten more minutes before the movie starts. Can you find us two seats? I'll grab treats from the concession stand.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Okay.<br /><span class =\"strong\">Clerk</span>: Can I help you?<br /><span class =\"strong\">Marco</span>: Yes, I'd like a large popcorn and a hot dog.<br /><span class =\"strong\">Clerk</span>: Any extra butter with the popcorn?", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn5le09ob06re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class =\"strong\">Marco</span>: No butter please. Can I get some nachos? Do you have any more pretzels?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Clerk</span>: We may have some left. Oh no, sorry, we're out of pretzels, but we have plenty of pizza.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Marco</span>: All right, then I'll have a slice of pizza.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Clerk</span>: Will that be all?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Marco</span>: No, I'd like some licorice and an ice cream sandwich.", "id": 2, "time": "16200", "image": "engenn5le09ob06re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class =\"strong\">Clerk</span>: Anything to drink?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Marco</span>: Yes, I'll take two large sodas.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Clerk</span>: That'll be $54.50.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Marco</span>: What?! That's crazy!<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Clerk</span>: If you look at the board, you can see all the prices are there. Do you still want all this?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Marco</span>: Just the sodas and popcorn.", "id": 3, "time": "37500", "image": "engenn5le09ob06re2img05.jpg"}]}}]}, {"id": 3, "type": "text", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "audio", "value": "engenn5le09ob06re6aud01"}]}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Vanessa Starts Dating Marco"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "What Shall We Get?"}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 9}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify and describe plans for the organization of events."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le09ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Will, May, Might"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Future tense (<span class =\"strong\">will</span>) to talk about actions in the future. You can also use the modals <span class =\"strong\">might</span> and <span class =\"strong\">may</span> to talk about possible actions in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The auxiliary <span class =\"strong\">will</span> goes before the verb. The short form is <span class=\"strong\">\u2018ll</span>.<br /><br />  You use the Future tense when you talk about the future, make offers or make predictions.<br /><br />  The modals <span class =\"strong\">might</span>   and <span class =\"strong\">may</span>   go before the verb.<br /><br />  They talk about future possibility or chance that something will happen.<br /><br /> <span class =\"strong\">Might</span>   means there is a smaller chance that something will happen (30%).<br /><br />  <span class =\"strong\">May</span> means there is a slightly greater chance that something will happen (50%)."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'll have just one of those, please. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "We might have a few hot dogs left. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "We may not have any salted butter though."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Quantifiers"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use a quantifier before a noun to indicate the amount or number of an item."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use quantifiers with both count and non-count nouns. You can use all of the quantifiers below with both count and non-count nouns."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\"> Quantifier </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\">Meaning</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"more<br /> less/fewer<br /> no/none<br /> any /not any<br /> some<br /> a lot of / lots of<br /> plenty of<br /> enough\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a larger number/amount<br /> a smaller number/amount<br /> 0<br /> to ask about / say there is no ...<br /> a small number/amount<br /> a very large number/amount<br /> more than you need<br /> as much as you need\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "There's plenty of popcorn in there!  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I don't want any butter on it. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "There is not enough butter on this."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "treat "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a tasty food that you do not get to eat very often "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm going to buy us some treats from the stand."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob06aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you hear at the movie theater. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "popcorn "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a kind of corn that bursts open when heated "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I love to eat popcorn with lots of butter."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob06aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hot dog "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a cooked sausage in a long piece of bread "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'd like one hot dog please."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob06aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "nachos"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "tortilla chips covered with cheese"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Can I get some nachos please?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob06aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pretzel"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a salty type of bread baked in the shape of a loose knot"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  Are there any pretzels left?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob06aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "licorice"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a long, thick red or black piece of chewy candy"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'd also like some licorice please. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob06aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ice cream sandwich"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "ice cream between two cookies"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I love eating ice cream sandwiches in the summer."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob06aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "soda"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a sweet carbonated drink "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Can I get two large sodas please?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob06aud08"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go on the internet or to a supermarket. Find a flyer for a supermarket."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a list of the food and drinks you see."}, {"type": "text", "content": "What items would you buy?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write 7-8 sentences about the items. Start your sentence with <span class=\"italic\">If I go shopping, I will buy ...</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use 4 quantifiers."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Proofread your sentences."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read them aloud to your partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write about food and drink."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about the quantities of food."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about possible actions in the future."}]}], "type": "sena"}